## 1. Executive Summary

This project implements an **emotion classification system** for short English text using a fine-tuned **DistilBERT** model on the public **Emotion** dataset (`dair-ai/emotion`). The work was carried out in **Google Colab**, following a standard NLP pipeline: data loading, exploratory analysis, tokenization, supervised fine-tuning, and quantitative evaluation on a test split.

An **optional extension** integrates **Meta SeamlessM4T v2** to translate English speech into multiple target languages (German, English, Turkish, Mandarin, Urdu, Arabic, Persian), demonstrating how translated text can be passed into the same emotion classifier for cross-lingual experimentation.

**Primary outcome:** a deployable text-to-emotion classifier over six categories (sadness, joy, love, anger, fear, surprise) with reproducible training via Hugging Face `Trainer`.

**Secondary outcome:** a prototype chain from **speech → translation → text emotion label**, useful as a foundation for multilingual affective computing applications.

